0,Kulango language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kulango_language,"There are two principal varieties distinct enough to be considered separate languages: the Kulango of Bondoukou (Bonduku), also known as Goutougo locally, and that of Bouna (Buna).","Kulango, Bondoukou",Niger-Congo
1,Kulango languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kulango_languages,The Kulango or Kulango–Lorhon languages are spoken principally in Ivory Coast. They were once classified as part of an expanded Gur (Voltaic) family and are now part of the Savannas proposal.,"Kulango, Bondoukou",Niger-Congo
